{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404550",
      "title": "Protecting Screens",
      "lectureOrder": 182,
      "videoOrder": 178,
      "sourceHash": "5030c001882835302ca8a8ae98ce88dda5d0a02eb29ff1b966f26029528af540",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.35,
          "end": 4.63,
          "en": "So how can we switch screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.63,
          "end": 7.37,
          "en": "based on the authentication status?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.37,
          "end": 9.7,
          "en": "This switching of screens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.7,
          "end": 13.56,
          "en": "or to be precise of entire screen setups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.56,
          "end": 16.58,
          "en": "and navigators in this case is sometimes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.58,
          "end": 21.01,
          "en": "also called route protection or screen protection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.01,
          "end": 24.61,
          "en": "It's called screen protection because we wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.61,
          "end": 29.01,
          "en": "that under no circumstances, certain screens can be reached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.01,
          "end": 30.963,
          "en": "if a certain condition is not met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.05,
          "end": 35.52,
          "en": "For example, we wanna make sure that under no circumstances",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.52,
          "end": 37.74,
          "en": "the Welcome Screen can be reached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.74,
          "end": 39.76,
          "en": "if the user is not logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.76,
          "end": 41.32,
          "en": "How is this achieved?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.32,
          "end": 45.46,
          "en": "By simply putting this screen into its own screen set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.46,
          "end": 48.29,
          "en": "into its own navigator in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.29,
          "end": 50.73,
          "en": "and only rendering this navigator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.73,
          "end": 52.453,
          "en": "if a certain condition is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.65,
          "end": 57.31,
          "en": "Please note that initially in our route app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.31,
          "end": 60.45,
          "en": "we only render the AuthStack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.45,
          "end": 63.563,
          "en": "We don't render the AuthenticatedStack at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.74,
          "end": 68.53,
          "en": "And in our app component, it is this navigation component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.53,
          "end": 71.36,
          "en": "This one here that only renders the AuthStack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.36,
          "end": 72.543,
          "en": "that is being rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.48,
          "end": 76.49,
          "en": "So initially there is no way of reaching the Welcome Screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.49,
          "end": 79.82,
          "en": "because this entire component that renders this navigator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.82,
          "end": 82.203,
          "en": "with that screen is not considered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.06,
          "end": 85.8,
          "en": "Now, we basically want to use state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.8,
          "end": 90.26,
          "en": "or context state to make sure that we basically swap",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.26,
          "end": 94.13,
          "en": "this AuthStack with the auth related routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.13,
          "end": 96.00999999999999,
          "en": "the auth related screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.00999999999999,
          "end": 98.1,
          "en": "for this AuthenticatedStack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.1,
          "end": 99.43,
          "en": "which holds the screens that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.43,
          "end": 101.58,
          "en": "are for authenticated users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.58,
          "end": 104.83,
          "en": "And therefore, once we switched to that different stack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.83,
          "end": 106.7,
          "en": "to this different screen set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.7,
          "end": 109.28,
          "en": "there won't be any way of going back to the login",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.28,
          "end": 111.9,
          "en": "or signup screens, which makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.9,
          "end": 115.46000000000001,
          "en": "because an authenticated user shouldn't be able to go there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.46000000000001,
          "end": 118.263,
          "en": "He or she is already authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.14,
          "end": 122.07,
          "en": "To achieve this, we wanna conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.07,
          "end": 125.32300000000001,
          "en": "use the Auth or AuthenticatedStack here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.3,
          "end": 128.57,
          "en": "To do that, we wanna use context here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.57,
          "end": 130.11,
          "en": "in the navigation component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.11,
          "end": 131.9,
          "en": "and in order to use it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.9,
          "end": 136.01,
          "en": "we actually should move our AuthContextProvider wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.01,
          "end": 137.57,
          "en": "out of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.57,
          "end": 140.43,
          "en": "Otherwise we can't use the context in this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.52,
          "end": 144.02,
          "en": "and wrap it here around navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.02,
          "end": 145.583,
          "en": "in the app component instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.15,
          "end": 149.43,
          "en": "Now, inside of the navigation component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.43,
          "end": 151.317,
          "en": "we can now useContext",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.388,
          "end": 154.89,
          "en": "so we can use the useContext hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.89,
          "end": 158.253,
          "en": "and we can't have into the AuthContext here now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.13,
          "end": 164.96,
          "en": "So now we imported useContext from react here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.96,
          "end": 169.28300000000002,
          "en": "and we import AuthContext from the AuthContext file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.24,
          "end": 172.35,
          "en": "And now we can use the context here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.35,
          "end": 174.4,
          "en": "in the navigation component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.4,
          "end": 176.513,
          "en": "get our AuthContext here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.7,
          "end": 181.58,
          "en": "and now conditionally render different stacks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.58,
          "end": 185.97,
          "en": "Right here, we can wrap AuthStack in curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.97,
          "end": 188.16,
          "en": "to render it dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.16,
          "end": 191.41,
          "en": "And I wanna check if not AuthContext",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.83,
          "end": 194.51,
          "en": "is authenticated is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.51,
          "end": 196.85,
          "en": "So if we're not authenticated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.85,
          "end": 199.14,
          "en": "then I wanna render the AuthStack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.14,
          "end": 202.2,
          "en": "which holds the login and sign up screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.2,
          "end": 206.61,
          "en": "On the other hand, if AuthContext is authenticated is true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 206.61,
          "end": 209.46699999999998,
          "en": "I wanna use my AuthenticatedStack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.41,
          "end": 213.94,
          "en": "So that other component that is defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.94,
          "end": 216.04,
          "en": "in this file that is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216.04,
          "end": 218.5,
          "en": "for rendering the Welcome Screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.5,
          "end": 221.63,
          "en": "And of course, we could have more screen registered in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.63,
          "end": 223.8,
          "en": "that require user authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.8,
          "end": 226.03,
          "en": "You can have any kind of navigator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.03,
          "end": 227.603,
          "en": "or screen setup in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 228.63,
          "end": 231.48,
          "en": "But we're now rendering totally different screen setups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.48,
          "end": 236.25,
          "en": "and navigators based on the authentication status of a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.25,
          "end": 239.11,
          "en": "And that makes sure that we protect screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 239.11,
          "end": 241.433,
          "en": "against unauthorized access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 242.38,
          "end": 243.69,
          "en": "And with all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.69,
          "end": 247.58,
          "en": "if we now save everything and we reload all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 247.58,
          "end": 251.763,
          "en": "if I go back and I enter correct credentials here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 253.03,
          "end": 256.04,
          "en": "you see we end up on this Welcome Screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.04,
          "end": 257.86,
          "en": "We also got a warning down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 257.86,
          "end": 259.86,
          "en": "about which will take care in a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.86,
          "end": 262.713,
          "en": "but we end up on this Welcome Screen here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.04,
          "end": 266.41,
          "en": "Now regarding this warning, we are getting this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.41,
          "end": 269.71,
          "en": "because in login screen, I'm setting IsAuthenticating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 269.71,
          "end": 273.39,
          "en": "to false here to exit this loading state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 273.39,
          "end": 274.5,
          "en": "But actually I do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 274.5,
          "end": 277.59000000000003,
          "en": "at the same time where this screen is removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 277.59000000000003,
          "end": 281.545,
          "en": "from the screen because we changed the navigation stacks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 281.545,
          "end": 283.58,
          "en": "and therefore a state update is performed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 283.58,
          "end": 286.51,
          "en": "for a component that's not rendered anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 286.51,
          "end": 288.67,
          "en": "which React doesn't like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 288.67,
          "end": 292.19,
          "en": "The solution is to only set IsAuthenticating to false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 292.19,
          "end": 295.84000000000003,
          "en": "in the error case where we don't leave the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 295.84000000000003,
          "end": 298.06,
          "en": "And that should get rid of the error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.06,
          "end": 301.16,
          "en": "We wanna do the same thing here for signing up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 301.16,
          "end": 302.77,
          "en": "only do this in the error case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 302.77,
          "end": 304.97,
          "en": "and move it into this catch block therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 306.56,
          "end": 307.953,
          "en": "With that, if we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 308.92,
          "end": 310.293,
          "en": "if we try this again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 312.8,
          "end": 316.05,
          "en": "we now switch to this page without any error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 316.05,
          "end": 316.99,
          "en": "And please note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 316.99,
          "end": 319.83,
          "en": "that this screen switching happens automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 319.83,
          "end": 322.56,
          "en": "when we switch to navigation stacks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 322.56,
          "end": 326.25,
          "en": "We don't need to call navigate or replace.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 326.25,
          "end": 328.82,
          "en": "We shouldn't call it actually instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 328.82,
          "end": 332.38,
          "en": "by simply swapping the navigation stacks here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 332.38,
          "end": 336.97,
          "en": "we automatically switch to the main screen of the new stacks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 336.97,
          "end": 339.13,
          "en": "of the stack that is now active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 339.13,
          "end": 340.61,
          "en": "And I'm saying stack all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 340.61,
          "end": 341.61,
          "en": "the same would be true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 341.61,
          "end": 344.31,
          "en": "if you would be using other navigators here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 344.31,
          "end": 347.27,
          "en": "So this is not exclusive to the stack navigator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 347.27,
          "end": 351,
          "en": "the idea justice that we swap screens as needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 351,
          "end": 353.78,
          "en": "We also don't have to swap entire navigators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 353.78,
          "end": 354.87,
          "en": "as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 354.87,
          "end": 358.21,
          "en": "We could also just be swapping some individual screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 358.21,
          "end": 360.51,
          "en": "or protecting some individual screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 360.51,
          "end": 363.21,
          "en": "by rendering individual screens dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 363.21,
          "end": 365.6,
          "en": "here, I'm just switching entire navigators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 365.6,
          "end": 368.493,
          "en": "to drive home that point that you can do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 369.6,
          "end": 372.42,
          "en": "Now with that, we are logged in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 372.42,
          "end": 375.83,
          "en": "and of course the same flow works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 375.83,
          "end": 378.6,
          "en": "if we are creating a new user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 378.6,
          "end": 382.71,
          "en": "So if you create a new user with a unused email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 382.71,
          "end": 385.29,
          "en": "if you would use the same email address as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 385.29,
          "end": 386.65,
          "en": "we would get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 387.55,
          "end": 390.19,
          "en": "actually we can check this real quick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 390.19,
          "end": 393.1,
          "en": "and use a used email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 393.1,
          "end": 396.2,
          "en": "Now we get an error, but now if we do sign up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 396.2,
          "end": 400.89,
          "en": "with a new email address, so if we create a new user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 402.06,
          "end": 405.40999999999997,
          "en": "we also end up on the Welcome Screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
